#{[17592186557416 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186557435 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557416 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557416 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=5 \\\\ 3x+ky &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557416 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4508cab0-6e88-59d6-a9c3-7b9fc61a9c9d" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557416 #edb/ref 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & k & 3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & k & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & k+6 & -12\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=5 \\\\ (k+6)y &=-12.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-6,$ then the second equation is $0=-12,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-6.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557419 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186557441 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557419 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557419 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=-4 \\\\ 2x+ky &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557419 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "550c7cdf-5810-56e4-b192-4674132b8147" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557419 #edb/ref 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -4 \\\\ 2 & k & -3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -4 \\\\ 2 & k & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & k+6 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=-4 \\\\ (k+6)y &=5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-6,$ then the second equation is $0=5,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-6.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557444 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186557423 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557444 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557444 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-5 \\\\ -2x+ky &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557444 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f4f00ddd-faa4-5195-9569-dbec2d0e2e6c" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557444 #edb/ref 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ -2 & k & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ -2 & k & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & k+4 & -10\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-5 \\\\ (k+4)y &=-10.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-4,$ then the second equation is $0=-10,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557445 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186115242.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557445 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "8ae9e325-9ab6-53e2-9f58-322c0a6527aa" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557520 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186557517 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557520 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557520 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-2y-4z+2w &=22 \\\\ 2x+y-z+8w &=16 \\\\ 2x+4w &=12.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557520 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4149b33c-f03c-5dc8-a587-d4628af75acd" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557520 #edb/ref 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}2 & -2 & -4 & 2 & 22 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 & 8 & 16 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 12\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}2 & -2 & -4 & 2 & 22 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 & 8 & 16 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 & 8 & 16 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 2 & -10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 2 & -10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -2 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(2){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2w &=6 \\\\ y+3w &=1 \\\\ z-w &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y$ and $z$, and we have one free variable, $w$. That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ and $z$ in terms of $w$.\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-2w+6 \\\\ y &=-3w+1 \\\\ z &=w-3 \\\\ w &=w,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $w$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2w+6 \\\\ -3w+1 \\\\ w-3 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557532 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186557505 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557532 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557532 #edb/ref 107